  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "North American West Coast CTD data(supports acoustics data), 1995-present",
  "description": "Raw CTD data taken in support of acoustics sampling, various locations, usually up to 3 weeks` duration, for several years. Some continuous at one depth for duration of sampling period, other profiles to 70 or 100m at 1 h or 3 h intervals for the duration of the sampling period.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Testing acoustical equipment; studying upper ocean processes.\n\nSupplemental information: Risk Justification: Data not well documented and requires knowledge to interpret. Risk of Loss: High Impact Justification: Data used for one time analysis. Impact of Loss: Low Recommended Action: Bring data to archives Additional Info: Data from Canadian ships are on the IOS archive; data from American ships are not on the archive.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23570791",
